IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`
IMPORT `sg-definitions`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), Part 11A, LAYER 1, third module: s 386AF (the register of controllers: when it must be kept, what
-- it must hold, who may see it, and the offences) and s 386AFA (the additional particulars when a company has no registrable controller,
-- or has one it cannot identify).
--
-- THE PRESCRIBED THINGS. The text leaves to regulations the particulars, the time, the manner, the form and the place (s 386AF(7), (8), (10)).
-- None of them is among the sources, so each is an input named for the fact. A prescribed period is a number of DAYS (assumed: the
-- regulations are not read; NOTES.md, fork F-AF4).
--
-- THE TIME LIMITS. The text counts "not later than 30 days after" (s 386AF(1), (4)) and "not later than 60 days after" (s 386AF(2), (3), (5), (6)).
-- Both are counted with `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` (sg-periods.l4): the last day is the day of the event plus
-- the number of days, and an act on any earlier day is in time too. The same function serves "within the prescribed time" (fork F-AF5).
--
-- READING A RESULT: see the header of sgn-application.l4. A timing function answers JUST TRUE (done in time), JUST FALSE (done late, or
-- not done and the last day has passed) or NOTHING (not done, and the last day has not yet passed).
--
-- THE APPOINTED DAY. "appointed day" is the date section 4 of the Companies and Limited Liability Partnerships (Miscellaneous Amendments)
-- Act 2024 commenced (s 386AF(14)). That Act is not a source, so the date is an input.

§ `Section 386AF: dates the section names, and the one counting helper`

-- s 386AF(1), (2), (4), (5): "31 March 2017".
`s 386AF(1) the day 31 March 2017` MEANS Date 31 3 2017

-- Helper for every time limit of this module and of sgn-notices.l4 and sgn-nominees.l4: was an act done in time?
-- JUST TRUE: done, on or before the last day. JUST FALSE: done after the last day, or not done and the date asked is after the last day.
-- NOTHING: not done, and the last day has not yet passed. It states no rule of its own; each provision that calls it carries the text.
GIVEN `the act has been done` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the act was done` IS A DATE
      `the day the time began to run` IS A DATE
      `the number of days allowed` IS A NUMBER
      `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386AF(8) timing: the act was done in time` MEANS
    IF `the act has been done`
    THEN JUST (`period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the day the time began to run` `the day the act was done` `the number of days allowed` Days)   -- FALSE-kind where the act was done late (a period the text fixes in its own words: the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (a))
    ELSE (IF `the date asked` GREATER THAN `period: the last day of a period after` `the day the time began to run` `the number of days allowed` Days
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (a period the text fixes in its own words: the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (a)): the last day has passed and the act is not done
          ELSE NOTHING)     -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the last day has not yet passed, so the text does not yet say the act is late

§ `Section 386AF(1) to (6): when the register must be kept`

-- (1): a company incorporated on or after 31 March 2017 but before the appointed day.
-- src:25666 | 386AF.—(1) A company incorporated on or after 31 March 2017
-- src:25667 | but before the appointed day, must keep a register of its registrable
-- src:25672 | controllers not later than 30 days after the date of the company’s
-- src:25673 | incorporation.
@ref s 386AF(1) (src:25666-25673)
GIVEN `the date the company was incorporated` IS A DATE
      `the appointed day under section 386AF(14)` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 386AF(1) the last day by which the company must have kept its register` MEANS
    IF    `the date the company was incorporated` AT LEAST `s 386AF(1) the day 31 March 2017`
       AND `the date the company was incorporated` LESS THAN `the appointed day under section 386AF(14)`
    THEN JUST (`period: the last day of a period after` `the date the company was incorporated` 30 Days)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (1) speaks of "a company incorporated on or after 31 March 2017 but before the appointed day"; another company is for (1A), (2) or (3)

-- (1A): a company incorporated on or after the appointed day: it must keep the register starting on the date of incorporation.
-- src:25679 | (1A) A company incorporated on or after the appointed day must
-- src:25680 | keep a register of its registrable controllers starting on the date of the
-- src:25681 | company’s incorporation.
@ref s 386AF(1A) (src:25679-25681)
GIVEN `the date the company was incorporated` IS A DATE
      `the appointed day under section 386AF(14)` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 386AF(1A) the day on which the company must start to keep its register` MEANS
    IF `the date the company was incorporated` AT LEAST `the appointed day under section 386AF(14)`
    THEN JUST `the date the company was incorporated`
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (1A) speaks of "a company incorporated on or after the appointed day"

-- (2): a company incorporated before 31 March 2017: "not later than 60 days after that date".
-- src:25685 | (2) A company incorporated before 31 March 2017 must keep a
-- src:25686 | register of its registrable controllers not later than 60 days after that
-- src:25687 | date.
@ref s 386AF(2) (src:25685-25687)
GIVEN `the date the company was incorporated` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 386AF(2) the last day by which the company must have kept its register` MEANS
    IF `the date the company was incorporated` LESS THAN `s 386AF(1) the day 31 March 2017`
    THEN JUST (`period: the last day of a period after` `s 386AF(1) the day 31 March 2017` 60 Days)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (2) speaks of "a company incorporated before 31 March 2017"

-- (3): a company that was not subject to the Part and later becomes subject to it: 60 days after the date the Part applies or re-applies.
-- src:25691 | (3) If a company that is not a company to which this Part applies
-- src:25692 | subsequently becomes a company to which this Part applies, the
-- src:25693 | company must keep a register of its registrable controllers not later
-- src:25694 | than 60 days after the date on which this Part applies or re‑applies to
-- src:25695 | the company.
@ref s 386AF(3) (src:25691-25695)
GIVEN `the company was not a company to which this Part applied and subsequently became one` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which this Part applies or re-applies to the company` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 386AF(3) the last day by which the company must have kept its register` MEANS
    IF `the company was not a company to which this Part applied and subsequently became one`
    THEN JUST (`period: the last day of a period after` `the date on which this Part applies or re-applies to the company` 60 Days)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (3) speaks of "a company that is not a company to which this Part applies" that "subsequently becomes" one

-- The four together for a company. Where (3) applies it governs; otherwise the date of incorporation picks (2), (1) or (1A) (fork F-AF1).
GIVEN `the company was not a company to which this Part applied and subsequently became one` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which this Part applies or re-applies to the company` IS A DATE
      `the date the company was incorporated` IS A DATE
      `the appointed day under section 386AF(14)` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 386AF(1), (1A), (2) and (3) the day by which the company must have kept its register` MEANS
    IF `the company was not a company to which this Part applied and subsequently became one`
    THEN `s 386AF(3) the last day by which the company must have kept its register` `the company was not a company to which this Part applied and subsequently became one` `the date on which this Part applies or re-applies to the company`
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 386AF(2) the last day by which the company must have kept its register` `the date the company was incorporated`
         WHEN JUST d THEN JUST d
         WHEN NOTHING THEN
             CONSIDER `s 386AF(1) the last day by which the company must have kept its register` `the date the company was incorporated` `the appointed day under section 386AF(14)`
             WHEN JUST d THEN JUST d
             WHEN NOTHING THEN `s 386AF(1A) the day on which the company must start to keep its register` `the date the company was incorporated` `the appointed day under section 386AF(14)`

-- Did the company keep its register in time? (JUST TRUE yes; JUST FALSE no; NOTHING not yet due.)
GIVEN `the company was not a company to which this Part applied and subsequently became one` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which this Part applies or re-applies to the company` IS A DATE
      `the date the company was incorporated` IS A DATE
      `the appointed day under section 386AF(14)` IS A DATE
      `the company has kept its register of registrable controllers` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the company started to keep its register` IS A DATE
      `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386AF(1), (1A), (2) and (3) the company has kept its register in time` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 386AF(1), (1A), (2) and (3) the day by which the company must have kept its register` `the company was not a company to which this Part applied and subsequently became one` `the date on which this Part applies or re-applies to the company` `the date the company was incorporated` `the appointed day under section 386AF(14)`
    WHEN JUST d THEN `s 386AF(8) timing: the act was done in time` `the company has kept its register of registrable controllers` `the day the company started to keep its register` d 0 `the date asked`   -- FALSE-kind where late: "must keep a register of its registrable controllers not later than 30 days after ..." (a period the text fixes in its own words: ruling (a))
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): none of subsections (1), (1A), (2) and (3) fits the facts

-- (4): a foreign company registered under Division 2 of Part 11 on or after 31 March 2017 but before the appointed day.
-- src:25699 | (4) A foreign company registered under Division 2 of Part 11 on or
-- src:25700 | after 31 March 2017 but before the appointed day, must keep a
-- src:25701 | register of its registrable controllers not later than 30 days after the
-- src:25702 | date of the foreign company’s registration.
@ref s 386AF(4) (src:25699-25702)
GIVEN `the date the foreign company was registered under Division 2 of Part 11` IS A DATE
      `the appointed day under section 386AF(14)` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 386AF(4) the last day by which the foreign company must have kept its register` MEANS
    IF    `the date the foreign company was registered under Division 2 of Part 11` AT LEAST `s 386AF(1) the day 31 March 2017`
       AND `the date the foreign company was registered under Division 2 of Part 11` LESS THAN `the appointed day under section 386AF(14)`
    THEN JUST (`period: the last day of a period after` `the date the foreign company was registered under Division 2 of Part 11` 30 Days)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (4) speaks of a foreign company registered on or after 31 March 2017 but before the appointed day

-- (4A): registered on or after the appointed day: it must keep the register starting on the date of registration.
-- src:25708 | (4A) A foreign company registered under Division 2 of Part 11 on
-- src:25709 | or after the appointed day must keep a register of its registrable
-- src:25710 | controllers starting on the date of the foreign company’s registration.
@ref s 386AF(4A) (src:25708-25710)
GIVEN `the date the foreign company was registered under Division 2 of Part 11` IS A DATE
      `the appointed day under section 386AF(14)` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 386AF(4A) the day on which the foreign company must start to keep its register` MEANS
    IF `the date the foreign company was registered under Division 2 of Part 11` AT LEAST `the appointed day under section 386AF(14)`
    THEN JUST `the date the foreign company was registered under Division 2 of Part 11`
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (4A) speaks of a foreign company registered on or after the appointed day

-- (5): registered before 31 March 2017 ("Part XI" is the printed spelling of Part 11): "not later than 60 days after that date".
-- src:25714 | (5) A foreign company registered under Division 2 of Part XI
-- src:25715 | before 31 March 2017 must keep a register of its registrable
-- src:25716 | controllers not later than 60 days after that date.
@ref s 386AF(5) (src:25714-25716)
GIVEN `the date the foreign company was registered under Division 2 of Part 11` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 386AF(5) the last day by which the foreign company must have kept its register` MEANS
    IF `the date the foreign company was registered under Division 2 of Part 11` LESS THAN `s 386AF(1) the day 31 March 2017`
    THEN JUST (`period: the last day of a period after` `s 386AF(1) the day 31 March 2017` 60 Days)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (5) speaks of a foreign company registered before 31 March 2017

-- (6): a foreign company that becomes subject to the Part: 60 days after the date the Part applies or re-applies.
-- src:25720 | (6) If a foreign company that is not a foreign company to which this
-- src:25721 | Part applies subsequently becomes a foreign company to which this
-- src:25722 | Part applies, the foreign company must keep a register of its
-- src:25723 | registrable controllers not later than 60 days after the date on which
-- src:25724 | this Part applies or re‑applies to the foreign company.
@ref s 386AF(6) (src:25720-25724)
GIVEN `the foreign company was not a foreign company to which this Part applied and subsequently became one` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which this Part applies or re-applies to the foreign company` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 386AF(6) the last day by which the foreign company must have kept its register` MEANS
    IF `the foreign company was not a foreign company to which this Part applied and subsequently became one`
    THEN JUST (`period: the last day of a period after` `the date on which this Part applies or re-applies to the foreign company` 60 Days)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (6) speaks of a foreign company "that is not a foreign company to which this Part applies" that "subsequently becomes" one

GIVEN `the foreign company was not a foreign company to which this Part applied and subsequently became one` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which this Part applies or re-applies to the foreign company` IS A DATE
      `the date the foreign company was registered under Division 2 of Part 11` IS A DATE
      `the appointed day under section 386AF(14)` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 386AF(4), (4A), (5) and (6) the day by which the foreign company must have kept its register` MEANS
    IF `the foreign company was not a foreign company to which this Part applied and subsequently became one`
    THEN `s 386AF(6) the last day by which the foreign company must have kept its register` `the foreign company was not a foreign company to which this Part applied and subsequently became one` `the date on which this Part applies or re-applies to the foreign company`
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 386AF(5) the last day by which the foreign company must have kept its register` `the date the foreign company was registered under Division 2 of Part 11`
         WHEN JUST d THEN JUST d
         WHEN NOTHING THEN
             CONSIDER `s 386AF(4) the last day by which the foreign company must have kept its register` `the date the foreign company was registered under Division 2 of Part 11` `the appointed day under section 386AF(14)`
             WHEN JUST d THEN JUST d
             WHEN NOTHING THEN `s 386AF(4A) the day on which the foreign company must start to keep its register` `the date the foreign company was registered under Division 2 of Part 11` `the appointed day under section 386AF(14)`

GIVEN `the foreign company was not a foreign company to which this Part applied and subsequently became one` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which this Part applies or re-applies to the foreign company` IS A DATE
      `the date the foreign company was registered under Division 2 of Part 11` IS A DATE
      `the appointed day under section 386AF(14)` IS A DATE
      `the foreign company has kept its register of registrable controllers` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the foreign company started to keep its register` IS A DATE
      `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386AF(4), (4A), (5) and (6) the foreign company has kept its register in time` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 386AF(4), (4A), (5) and (6) the day by which the foreign company must have kept its register` `the foreign company was not a foreign company to which this Part applied and subsequently became one` `the date on which this Part applies or re-applies to the foreign company` `the date the foreign company was registered under Division 2 of Part 11` `the appointed day under section 386AF(14)`
    WHEN JUST d THEN `s 386AF(8) timing: the act was done in time` `the foreign company has kept its register of registrable controllers` `the day the foreign company started to keep its register` d 0 `the date asked`   -- FALSE-kind where late: "must keep a register of its registrable controllers not later than 30 days after ..." (a period the text fixes in its own words: ruling (a))
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): none of subsections (4), (4A), (5) and (6) fits the facts

§ `Section 386AF(1) to (6): the duty to keep the register, as regulative rules`

-- The party is the company or the foreign company (the core's Party: Company, or `Foreign company`). The clock of a trace counts DAYS from
-- the day the time begins to run: the date of incorporation or registration (day 0) for (1) and (4); 31 March 2017 for (2) and (5); the day the Part
-- applies or re-applies for (3) and (6). An act on day 30 (or 60) is in time ("not later than"); on day 31 (or 61) it is late.
DECLARE `s 386AF act` IS ONE OF
    `s 386AF(1) to (6) keep a register of its registrable controllers`
    `s 386AF(7)(a) ensure that the register contains the prescribed particulars of its registrable individual controllers and registrable corporate controllers`
    `s 386AF(7)(aa) ensure that the register contains the note and prescribed particulars required under section 386AFA(3), if applicable`
    `s 386AF(7)(b) ensure that the register is updated if any change to the prescribed particulars occurs`
    `s 386AF(7)(c) ensure that the register is kept in the prescribed form and at the prescribed place`
    `s 386AF(8) enter the particulars in the register and update the register`
    `s 386AF(9)(a) enter or update the particulars of a controller after the controller has confirmed them`
    `s 386AF(9)(b) enter or update the particulars of a controller with a note that they have not been confirmed by the controller`
    `s 386AF(11) disclose the register or any particulars in it, or make it available for inspection, to a member of the public`

-- src:25666 | 386AF.—(1) A company incorporated on or after 31 March 2017
-- src:25667 | but before the appointed day, must keep a register of its registrable
-- src:25672 | controllers not later than 30 days after the date of the company’s
-- src:25673 | incorporation.
@ref s 386AF(1) (src:25666-25673)
GIVEN `the company or foreign company` IS A Party
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 386AF act`
`s 386AF(1) a company incorporated on or after 31 March 2017 but before the appointed day must keep a register not later than 30 days after incorporation` MEANS
    PARTY `the company or foreign company`
    MUST `s 386AF(1) to (6) keep a register of its registrable controllers`
    WITHIN 30
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the company or foreign company` BECAUSE "the company did not keep a register of its registrable controllers not later than 30 days after its incorporation (s 386AF(1), (12))"

-- src:25679 | (1A) A company incorporated on or after the appointed day must
-- src:25680 | keep a register of its registrable controllers starting on the date of the
-- src:25681 | company’s incorporation.
@ref s 386AF(1A) (src:25679-25681)
GIVEN `the company or foreign company` IS A Party
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 386AF act`
`s 386AF(1A) a company incorporated on or after the appointed day must keep a register starting on the date of incorporation` MEANS
    PARTY `the company or foreign company`
    MUST `s 386AF(1) to (6) keep a register of its registrable controllers`
    WITHIN 0
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the company or foreign company` BECAUSE "the company did not keep a register of its registrable controllers starting on the date of its incorporation (s 386AF(1A), (12))"

