-- (8): enter the particulars and update the register "within the prescribed time and in the prescribed manner".
-- src:25751 | (8) A company or foreign company must enter the particulars in its
-- src:25752 | register and update the register within the prescribed time and in the
-- src:25753 | prescribed manner.
@ref s 386AF(8) (src:25751-25753)
GIVEN `the company or foreign company has entered the particulars or updated the register` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the company or foreign company entered the particulars or updated the register` IS A DATE
      `the day from which the prescribed time runs` IS A DATE
      `the prescribed time, in days` IS A NUMBER
      `the particulars were entered or the register was updated in the prescribed manner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386AF(8) the company or foreign company has entered the particulars and updated the register in time and in the prescribed manner` MEANS
    IF `the company or foreign company has entered the particulars or updated the register` AND (NOT `the particulars were entered or the register was updated in the prescribed manner`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must enter the particulars in its register and update the register within the prescribed time and in the prescribed manner" (done, but not in the prescribed manner)
    ELSE `s 386AF(8) timing: the act was done in time` `the company or foreign company has entered the particulars or updated the register` `the day the company or foreign company entered the particulars or updated the register` `the day from which the prescribed time runs` `the prescribed time, in days` `the date asked`   -- FALSE-kind where late (a period the text fixes in its own words: ruling (a)); NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording) while the prescribed time has not run out

-- src:25751 | (8) A company or foreign company must enter the particulars in its
-- src:25752 | register and update the register within the prescribed time and in the
-- src:25753 | prescribed manner.
@ref s 386AF(8) (src:25751-25753)
GIVEN `the company or foreign company` IS A Party
      `the prescribed time, in days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 386AF act`
`s 386AF(8) a company or foreign company must enter the particulars and update its register within the prescribed time` MEANS
    PARTY `the company or foreign company`
    MUST `s 386AF(8) enter the particulars in the register and update the register`
    WITHIN `the prescribed time, in days`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the company or foreign company` BECAUSE "the company did not enter the particulars in its register and update it within the prescribed time (s 386AF(8), (12)(b))"

-- (9): enter or update after the controller confirms; or, with no confirmation, enter or update with a note.
-- The subsection fixes no time of its own (s 386AF(8) does), so "not yet entered" is not a breach (NOTHING).
-- src:25757 | (9) A company or foreign company must —
-- src:25759 | (a) enter the particulars of any controller in its register, or
-- src:25760 | update the particulars of that controller in the register, after
-- src:25761 | the particulars of that controller are confirmed by the
-- src:25762 | controller; or
-- src:25764 | (b) if the company or foreign company does not receive the
-- src:25765 | controller’s confirmation, enter or update the particulars
-- src:25766 | with a note indicating that the particulars have not been
-- src:25767 | confirmed by the controller.
@ref s 386AF(9) (src:25757-25767)
GIVEN `the controller has confirmed the particulars` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company or foreign company has entered or updated the particulars in its register` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the entry or update carries a note that the particulars have not been confirmed by the controller` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386AF(9) the company or foreign company has done what the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the company or foreign company has entered or updated the particulars in its register`
    THEN (IF `the controller has confirmed the particulars`
          THEN JUST TRUE                                                    -- paragraph (a): entered or updated after the controller confirmed them
          ELSE (IF `the entry or update carries a note that the particulars have not been confirmed by the controller`
                THEN JUST TRUE                                              -- paragraph (b): no confirmation, entered with the note
                ELSE JUST FALSE))   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) if the company or foreign company does not receive the controller's confirmation, enter or update the particulars with a note indicating that the particulars have not been confirmed by the controller" (entered without confirmation and without the note)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (9) fixes no time; the time is "the prescribed time" of subsection (8), so an entry not yet made is not yet a failure

-- src:25757 | (9) A company or foreign company must —
-- src:25759 | (a) enter the particulars of any controller in its register, or
-- src:25760 | update the particulars of that controller in the register, after
-- src:25761 | the particulars of that controller are confirmed by the
-- src:25762 | controller; or
@ref s 386AF(9)(a) (src:25757-25762)
GIVEN `the company or foreign company` IS A Party
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 386AF act`
`s 386AF(9)(a) a company or foreign company must enter or update the particulars of a controller after the controller confirms them` MEANS
    PARTY `the company or foreign company`
    MUST `s 386AF(9)(a) enter or update the particulars of a controller after the controller has confirmed them`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: no deadline is modelled for this duty; dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY `the company or foreign company` BECAUSE "the company did not enter or update the particulars of a controller after the controller confirmed them (s 386AF(9)(a), (12)(b))" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md) [class: other; see notes]

-- src:25764 | (b) if the company or foreign company does not receive the
-- src:25765 | controller’s confirmation, enter or update the particulars
-- src:25766 | with a note indicating that the particulars have not been
-- src:25767 | confirmed by the controller.
@ref s 386AF(9)(b) (src:25764-25767)
GIVEN `the company or foreign company` IS A Party
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 386AF act`
`s 386AF(9)(b) a company or foreign company that does not receive the confirmation must enter or update the particulars with a note` MEANS
    PARTY `the company or foreign company`
    MUST `s 386AF(9)(b) enter or update the particulars of a controller with a note that they have not been confirmed by the controller`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: no deadline is modelled for this duty; dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY `the company or foreign company` BECAUSE "the company did not enter or update the particulars with a note that the controller had not confirmed them (s 386AF(9)(b), (12)(b))" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md) [class: other; see notes]

-- (10): the confirmation for (9)(a) must be given by the controller in the prescribed manner.
-- src:25771 | (10) For the purposes of subsection (9)(a), the particulars of the
-- src:25772 | controller to be entered, or updated, in a register must be confirmed
-- src:25773 | by the controller in the prescribed manner.
@ref s 386AF(10) (src:25771-25773)
GIVEN `the controller has confirmed the particulars in the prescribed manner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386AF(10) the controller's confirmation is a confirmation for the purposes of subsection (9)(a)` MEANS
    IF `the controller has confirmed the particulars in the prescribed manner`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the particulars of the controller to be entered, or updated, in a register must be confirmed by the controller in the prescribed manner" (a requirement not met)

§ `Section 386AF(11): the register is not to be shown to the public`

-- (11): "Subject to section 386AM" the company must not disclose the register or its particulars, or make it available for inspection, to any member of the public.
-- Read as the bar: JUST TRUE the bar applies to this person; JUST FALSE a requirement under s 386AM lifts it; NOTHING the person is not a member of the public (fork F-AF3).
-- src:25777 | (11) Subject to section 386AM, a company or foreign company
-- src:25778 | must not disclose, or make available for inspection, a register or any
-- src:25779 | particulars contained in the register to any member of the public.
@ref s 386AF(11) (src:25777-25779)
GIVEN `the person is a member of the public` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure or inspection is a requirement or the exercise of a power under section 386AM` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386AF(11) the company or foreign company is barred from disclosing the register to the person` MEANS
    IF `the disclosure or inspection is a requirement or the exercise of a power under section 386AM`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subject to section 386AM, a company or foreign company must not disclose ..." (an exception in the text's own words, a plain variant of "except": the bar does not apply to what section 386AM requires)
    ELSE (IF `the person is a member of the public`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar is "to any member of the public" (the scope limit of the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (c)); it says nothing of disclosure to anyone else

-- src:25777 | (11) Subject to section 386AM, a company or foreign company
-- src:25778 | must not disclose, or make available for inspection, a register or any
-- src:25779 | particulars contained in the register to any member of the public.
@ref s 386AF(11) (src:25777-25779)
GIVEN `the company or foreign company` IS A Party
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 386AF act`
`s 386AF(11) a company or foreign company must not disclose the register to a member of the public` MEANS
    PARTY `the company or foreign company`
    SHANT `s 386AF(11) disclose the register or any particulars in it, or make it available for inspection, to a member of the public`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the company or foreign company` BECAUSE "the company disclosed the register or its particulars, or made it available for inspection, to a member of the public (s 386AF(11), (12)(b))"

§ `Section 386AF(12) and (13): the offences, and (14) the appointed day`

-- (12): a company that fails to comply with (1), (1A), (2) or (3), or (7), (8), (9) or (11), and every officer in default, are each guilty; fine up to $25,000.
-- "officer who is in default" is the s 408(3) phrase (another part's range): an officer who knowingly and wilfully is guilty of the offence or authorises or permits it.
-- src:25786 | (12) If a company fails to comply with —
-- src:25788 | (a) subsection (1), (1A), (2) or (3), whichever is applicable; or
-- src:25792 | (b) subsection (7), (8), (9) or (11),
-- src:25794 | the company, and every officer of the company who is in default,
-- src:25795 | shall each be guilty of an offence and shall each be liable on
-- src:25796 | conviction to a fine not exceeding $25,000.
@ref s 386AF(12) (src:25786-25796)
GIVEN `the company fails to comply with subsection (1), (1A), (2) or (3), whichever is applicable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company fails to comply with subsection (7), (8), (9) or (11)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386AF(12) the company is guilty of the offence` MEANS
    IF `the company fails to comply with subsection (1), (1A), (2) or (3), whichever is applicable` OR `the company fails to comply with subsection (7), (8), (9) or (11)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the provision's own question; split site (i), fork line F-AF6): "If a company fails to comply with — (a) subsection (1), (1A), (2) or (3), whichever is applicable; or (b) subsection (7), (8), (9) or (11), the company ... shall each be guilty of an offence" (no failure, so this subsection makes the company guilty of nothing)

-- src:25786 | (12) If a company fails to comply with —
-- src:25788 | (a) subsection (1), (1A), (2) or (3), whichever is applicable; or
-- src:25792 | (b) subsection (7), (8), (9) or (11),
-- src:25794 | the company, and every officer of the company who is in default,
-- src:25795 | shall each be guilty of an offence and shall each be liable on
-- src:25796 | conviction to a fine not exceeding $25,000.
@ref s 386AF(12) (src:25786-25796)
GIVEN `the company fails to comply with subsection (1), (1A), (2) or (3), whichever is applicable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company fails to comply with subsection (7), (8), (9) or (11)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer of the company who is in default, as section 408(3) gives that meaning` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386AF(12) the officer of the company is guilty of the offence` MEANS
    IF    (`the company fails to comply with subsection (1), (1A), (2) or (3), whichever is applicable` OR `the company fails to comply with subsection (7), (8), (9) or (11)`)
       AND `the person is an officer of the company who is in default, as section 408(3) gives that meaning`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the provision's own question; split site (i), fork line F-AF6): "the company, and every officer of the company who is in default, shall each be guilty of an offence" (the company did not fail, or the person is not an officer in default)

-- src:25786 | (12) If a company fails to comply with —
-- src:25788 | (a) subsection (1), (1A), (2) or (3), whichever is applicable; or
-- src:25792 | (b) subsection (7), (8), (9) or (11),
-- src:25794 | the company, and every officer of the company who is in default,
-- src:25795 | shall each be guilty of an offence and shall each be liable on
-- src:25796 | conviction to a fine not exceeding $25,000.
@ref s 386AF(12) (src:25786-25796)
GIVEN `the company fails to comply with subsection (1), (1A), (2) or (3), whichever is applicable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company fails to comply with subsection (7), (8), (9) or (11)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer of the company who is in default, as section 408(3) gives that meaning` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 386AF(12) the most the company or an officer in default may be sentenced to on conviction` MEANS
    IF (IF `the person is the company`
        THEN `s 386AF(12) the company is guilty of the offence` `the company fails to comply with subsection (1), (1A), (2) or (3), whichever is applicable` `the company fails to comply with subsection (7), (8), (9) or (11)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        ELSE `s 386AF(12) the officer of the company is guilty of the offence` `the company fails to comply with subsection (1), (1A), (2) or (3), whichever is applicable` `the company fails to comply with subsection (7), (8), (9) or (11)` `the person is an officer of the company who is in default, as section 408(3) gives that meaning` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST (Penalty OF 25000, 0, FALSE, FALSE)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection states a penalty only for the person it makes guilty

