§ `Section 386AFA: additional particulars where there is no registrable controller, or one that cannot be identified`

-- (1): the section applies where the company knows, or has reasonable grounds to believe, (a) it has no registrable controller or (b) it has one it cannot identify.
-- src:25826 | 386AFA.—(1) This section applies where a company or foreign
-- src:25827 | company knows, or has reasonable grounds to believe —
-- src:25829 | (a) that the company or foreign company has no registrable
-- src:25830 | controller; or
-- src:25832 | (b) that the company or foreign company has a registrable
-- src:25833 | controller but has not been able to identify the registrable
-- src:25834 | controller.
@ref s 386AFA(1) (src:25826-25834)
GIVEN `the company or foreign company knows, or has reasonable grounds to believe, that it has no registrable controller` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company or foreign company knows, or has reasonable grounds to believe, that it has a registrable controller but has not been able to identify the registrable controller` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386AFA(1) this section applies to the company or foreign company` MEANS
    IF    `the company or foreign company knows, or has reasonable grounds to believe, that it has no registrable controller`
       OR `the company or foreign company knows, or has reasonable grounds to believe, that it has a registrable controller but has not been able to identify the registrable controller`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies where a company or foreign company knows, or has reasonable grounds to believe — (a) ...; or (b) ..." (a failed "where": the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b); fork line F-AFA1)

-- (8): the definitions the section uses. "chief executive officer" is s 4(1)'s (sg-definitions.l4), with "the foreign company" read for "the company" for a foreign company.
-- src:25920 | (8) In this section —
-- src:25922 | “chief executive officer” —
-- src:25924 | (a) in relation to a company, has the meaning given by
-- src:25925 | section 4(1); and
-- src:25927 | (b) in relation to a foreign company, has the meaning
-- src:25928 | given by section 4(1), subject to the modification that
-- src:25929 | each reference to a company is a reference to the
-- src:25930 | foreign company;
@ref s 386AFA(8) "chief executive officer" (src:25920-25930)
GIVEN `the person is in direct employment of, or acting for or by arrangement with, the company or foreign company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is principally responsible for the management and conduct of the business of the company or foreign company, or part of the business of the company or foreign company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386AFA(8) "chief executive officer" the person is a chief executive officer of the company or foreign company` MEANS
    `s 4(1) "chief executive officer" the person is a chief executive officer of the company` `the person is in direct employment of, or acting for or by arrangement with, the company or foreign company` `the person is principally responsible for the management and conduct of the business of the company or foreign company, or part of the business of the company or foreign company`   -- JUST FALSE where s 4(1) says no in its own words ("means"), with "the foreign company" read for "the company" as paragraph (b) requires

-- src:25932 | “director with executive control”, in relation to a company or
-- src:25933 | foreign company, means a director of the company or foreign
-- src:25934 | company who exercises executive control over the daily or
-- src:25939 | regular affairs of the company or foreign company through a
-- src:25940 | senior management position.
@ref s 386AFA(8) "director with executive control" (src:25932-25940)
GIVEN `the person is a director of the company or foreign company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person exercises executive control over the daily or regular affairs of the company or foreign company through a senior management position` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386AFA(8) "director with executive control" the person is a director with executive control` MEANS
    IF `the person is a director of the company or foreign company` AND `the person exercises executive control over the daily or regular affairs of the company or foreign company through a senior management position`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“director with executive control”, in relation to a company or foreign company, means a director of the company or foreign company who exercises executive control over the daily or regular affairs of the company or foreign company through a senior management position"

-- (2): where the section applies, each director with executive control and each chief executive officer is, subject to subsection (9), taken to be a registrable controller.
-- src:25836 | (2) Where this section applies, each director with executive control
-- src:25837 | and each chief executive officer of the company or foreign company
-- src:25838 | is, subject to subsection (9), taken to be a registrable controller of the
-- src:25839 | company or foreign company for the purposes of this Part.
@ref s 386AFA(2) (src:25836-25839)
GIVEN `this section applies to the company or foreign company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a director with executive control of the company or foreign company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a chief executive officer of the company or foreign company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386AFA(2) the person is taken to be a registrable controller of the company or foreign company for the purposes of this Part` MEANS
    IF NOT `this section applies to the company or foreign company`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where this section applies, each director with executive control and each chief executive officer ... is ... taken to be a registrable controller" (a failed "where": the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b); fork line F-AFA1)
    ELSE (IF `the person is a director with executive control of the company or foreign company` OR `the person is a chief executive officer of the company or foreign company`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection names directors with executive control and chief executive officers, with no "only"

-- (3): where the section applies, the company must enter in its register a note (a) and the prescribed particulars (b). The subsection fixes no time (subsection (4) does).
-- src:25844 | (3) Where this section applies, the company or foreign company
-- src:25845 | must enter the following in its register of controllers:
-- src:25847 | (a) a note stating —
-- src:25849 | (i) that the company or foreign company knows, or has
-- src:25850 | reasonable grounds to believe, as the case may be —
-- src:25852 | (A) that the company or foreign company has no
-- src:25853 | registrable controller; or
-- src:25855 | (B) that the company or foreign company has a
-- src:25856 | registrable controller but has not been able to
-- src:25857 | identify the registrable controller; and
-- src:25859 | (ii) that each director with executive control and each
-- src:25860 | chief executive officer of the company or foreign
-- src:25861 | company is taken to be a registrable controller of the
-- src:25862 | company or foreign company under subsection (2);
-- src:25864 | (b) the prescribed particulars of each director with executive
-- src:25865 | control and each chief executive officer of the company or
-- src:25866 | foreign company.
@ref s 386AFA(3) (src:25844-25866)
GIVEN `this section applies to the company or foreign company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company or foreign company has entered the note that subsection (3)(a) describes` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company or foreign company has entered the prescribed particulars of each director with executive control and each chief executive officer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386AFA(3) the company or foreign company has entered in its register what the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF NOT `this section applies to the company or foreign company`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where this section applies, the company or foreign company must enter the following in its register of controllers" (a failed "where": the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b); fork line F-AFA1)
    ELSE (IF `the company or foreign company has entered the note that subsection (3)(a) describes` AND `the company or foreign company has entered the prescribed particulars of each director with executive control and each chief executive officer`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (3) fixes no time for the entry; the time is the prescribed period of subsection (4), so an entry not yet made is not yet a failure

-- src:25844 | (3) Where this section applies, the company or foreign company
