GIVEN `the company or foreign company` IS A Party
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 386AFA act`
`s 386AFA(3) a company or foreign company to which the section applies must enter the note and the prescribed particulars` MEANS
    PARTY `the company or foreign company`
    MUST `s 386AFA(3) enter in the register of controllers the note and the prescribed particulars of each director with executive control and each chief executive officer`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: no deadline is modelled for this duty; dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY `the company or foreign company` BECAUSE "the company did not enter the note and the prescribed particulars in its register of controllers (s 386AFA(3), (7))" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md) [class: other; see notes]

-- (4): enter those matters within the prescribed period after (a) the date the company knows it has no registrable controller, or (b) the date it forms the opinion,
-- having taken the reasonable steps s 386AG(1) requires, that it cannot identify the registrable controller.
DECLARE `s 386AFA(4) case` IS ONE OF
    `s 386AFA(4)(a) the company or foreign company knows, or has reasonable grounds to believe, that it has no registrable controller`
    `s 386AFA(4)(b) the company or foreign company has a registrable controller it has not been able to identify`

-- src:25868 | (4) A company or foreign company must enter the matters
-- src:25869 | mentioned in subsection (3) in its register of controllers within the
-- src:25870 | prescribed period after —
-- src:25872 | (a) in the case of a company or foreign company that knows,
-- src:25873 | or has reasonable grounds to believe, that it has no
-- src:25874 | registrable controller — the date on which the company or
-- src:25875 | foreign company knows, or has reasonable grounds to
-- src:25876 | believe, that the company or foreign company has no
-- src:25877 | registrable controller; or
-- src:25879 | (b) in the case of a company or foreign company that knows,
-- src:25880 | or has reasonable grounds to believe, that it has a
-- src:25881 | registrable controller but has not been able to identify
-- src:25882 | the registrable controller — the date on which the company
-- src:25883 | or foreign company, having taken the reasonable steps
-- src:25884 | required by section 386AG(1), forms the opinion that it is
-- src:25885 | unable to identify the registrable controller.
@ref s 386AFA(4) (src:25868-25885)
GIVEN case IS A `s 386AFA(4) case`
      `the date on which the company or foreign company knows, or has reasonable grounds to believe, that it has no registrable controller` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the company or foreign company, having taken the reasonable steps required by section 386AG(1), forms the opinion that it is unable to identify the registrable controller` IS A DATE
      `the company or foreign company has entered the matters mentioned in subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the company or foreign company entered the matters mentioned in subsection (3)` IS A DATE
      `the prescribed period, in days` IS A NUMBER
      `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386AFA(4) the company or foreign company has entered the matters within the prescribed period` MEANS
    `s 386AF(8) timing: the act was done in time` `the company or foreign company has entered the matters mentioned in subsection (3)` `the day the company or foreign company entered the matters mentioned in subsection (3)`
        (CONSIDER case
         WHEN `s 386AFA(4)(a) the company or foreign company knows, or has reasonable grounds to believe, that it has no registrable controller` THEN `the date on which the company or foreign company knows, or has reasonable grounds to believe, that it has no registrable controller`
         WHEN `s 386AFA(4)(b) the company or foreign company has a registrable controller it has not been able to identify` THEN `the date on which the company or foreign company, having taken the reasonable steps required by section 386AG(1), forms the opinion that it is unable to identify the registrable controller`)
        `the prescribed period, in days` `the date asked`   -- FALSE-kind where late ("must enter the matters mentioned in subsection (3) in its register of controllers within the prescribed period after ...": a period the text fixes in its own words: ruling (a)); NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording) while the period has not run out

DECLARE `s 386AFA act` IS ONE OF
    `s 386AFA(3) enter in the register of controllers the note and the prescribed particulars of each director with executive control and each chief executive officer`
    `s 386AFA(5) update the register of controllers to reflect a change in the particulars entered under subsection (3)(b)`
    `s 386AFA(6) enter in the register of controllers the note that subsection (6) describes`

